        "id": 119932,
        "name": "dwetuski",
        "username": "dwetuski",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/3e96dc/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-11-02T09:24:07.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Ah, good catch. &nbsp;If they could be returned to the deck, it would explicitly say that. &nbsp;I knew something felt off. &nbsp;Thanks.</p><p>Although, if we're really going to read the card literally, the word \"may\" still implies that making the choice is optional. &nbsp;Otherwise, it would say something like, \"That player reveals the top 2 cards of their deck and chooses to play, draw, or discard each of them in any order.\" &nbsp;So, rules as written, if the player chooses not to do any of those 3 things to one or both cards, then the card(s) would remain revealed and effectively out of play for the rest of the game. &nbsp;Of course, it's hard to imagine that that's rules as intended, and I certainly wouldn't play it that way, but literally, that's what it says.</p>",
