        "raw": "<p>Ah, good catch. &nbsp;If they could be returned to the deck, it would explicitly say that. &nbsp;I knew something felt off. &nbsp;Thanks.</p><p>Although, if we&#39;re really going to read the card literally, the word &quot;may&quot; still implies that making the choice is optional. &nbsp;Otherwise, it would say something like, &quot;That player reveals the top 2 cards of their deck and chooses to play, draw, or discard each of them in any order.&quot; &nbsp;So, rules as written, if the player chooses not to do any of those 3 things to one or both cards, then the card(s) would remain revealed and effectively out of play for the rest of the game. &nbsp;Of course, it&#39;s hard to imagine that that&#39;s rules as intended, and I certainly wouldn&#39;t play it that way, but literally, that&#39;s what it says.</p>",
