      {
        "id": 119933,
        "name": "AlexxKay",
        "username": "AlexxKay",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/59ef9b/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-11-02T16:08:14.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I thought for a while that I had a counterargument:&nbsp; Tachyon's base power (Rapid Recon).&nbsp; If read the way Matchstickman suggests, Tachyon would *always* have to discard the top card, and that doesn't seem right.&nbsp; But her power doesn't actually say \"reveal\", it says \"look at\".&nbsp; So the card is still technically on top of the deck (even if the player actually picked it up to look at), and doing a no-op doesn't leave any cards in an untenable state.</p><p>This Reveal/Look At distinction can also be significant when fighting Ambuscade.&nbsp; If I understand correctly, \"reveal\" actions cause traps underneath the revealed cards to go off, whereas \"look at\" actions do not.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:53:16.177Z",
