        "raw": "<p>I thought for a while that I had a counterargument:&nbsp; Tachyon&#39;s base power (Rapid Recon).&nbsp; If read the way Matchstickman suggests, Tachyon would *always* have to discard the top card, and that doesn&#39;t seem right.&nbsp; But her power doesn&#39;t actually say &quot;reveal&quot;, it says &quot;look at&quot;.&nbsp; So the card is still technically on top of the deck (even if the player actually picked it up to look at), and doing a no-op doesn&#39;t leave any cards in an untenable state.</p><p>This Reveal/Look At distinction can also be significant when fighting Ambuscade.&nbsp; If I understand correctly, &quot;reveal&quot; actions cause traps underneath the revealed cards to go off, whereas &quot;look at&quot; actions do not.</p>",
